1
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:52,880
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,930
[Episode 11]

3
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,240
Aren't there peeled ones here?

4
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,420
You'll break your little teeth.

5
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:06,420
Is it tasty?

6
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:07,420
Yes.

7
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,000
Listen,

8
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:11,850
clear this table

9
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:13,190
and bring the food over here.

10
00:01:13,539 --> 00:01:14,650
Eating here again?

11
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:16,050
The kid is watching TV.

12
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:22,789
Tasty, right?

13
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,060
Move aside.

14
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:27,370
Okay.

15
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:28,990
You're blocking his view of the TV.

16
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,400
Qiu, don't eat too many snacks.

17
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:33,420
-Or you won't want to have the meal later.
-Let him eat.

18
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:34,430
What's it to you?

19
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:35,479
Hurry up and clean up.

20
00:01:41,259 --> 00:01:41,979
I'm back.

21
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:43,950
Your grandpa is back.

22
00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:44,780
Grandpa.

23
00:01:45,979 --> 00:01:47,570
On the road ahead,

24
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,340
another person got run over.

25
00:01:50,979 --> 00:01:53,600
Man, it was brutal.

26
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:55,560
He was crushed flat.

27
00:01:56,009 --> 00:01:57,660
Blood everywhere.

28
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:00,420
How many cars must have run over him?

29
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,260
I don't know.

30
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:03,460
They found over a dozen cars

31
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:05,060
with blood on their tires,

32
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:07,590
but they all said
they weren't the first to hit him.

33
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,130
It was dark.

34
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,690
They didn't see

35
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:13,000
someone was in the middle of the road.

36
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:15,300
So tragic.

37
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,190
So pitiful.

38
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:17,950
Give me the remote.

39
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,700
You got another bracelet?

40
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:22,579
You're always decked in gold and silver.

41
00:02:22,579 --> 00:02:24,150
Are you worried others won't know

42
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:25,780
where our family's money comes from?

43
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:28,500
My son bought it for me.

44
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:30,040
Just show off.

45
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,280
Bring some water.

46
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:33,180
For a case like this,

47
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:34,600
what would the verdict be?

48
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,280
What else could it be?

49
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,470
No evidence.

50
00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:39,550
Pay some money and that's it.

51
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:42,180
Why would anyone
run to the middle of the road

52
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:42,800
for no reason?

53
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:43,620
Probably he got drunk.

54
00:02:44,210 --> 00:02:45,500
It's all because of alcohol.

55
00:02:47,090 --> 00:02:49,340
Um, the Sun family next door

56
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:50,970
just had another chubby grandson.

57
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,390
Two now?

58
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:54,800
Look at them.

59
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,590
Look at them.

60
00:02:58,410 --> 00:03:00,860
How do they have such good fortune?

61
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,920
A thriving family
with lots of children and grandchildren.

62
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:06,310
Look.

63
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:07,930
T-This.

64
00:03:07,930 --> 00:03:09,500
Everything's so salty.

65
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,760
Th-These heavy dishes

66
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,120
are so greasy.

67
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:14,360
The TV says

68
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,690
stewed meat

69
00:03:16,690 --> 00:03:18,480
has... what's it called?

70
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,500
Purines.

71
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,410
Right, purines.

72
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:21,370
We should eat less of it.

73
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:23,790
Make a fish

74
00:03:24,630 --> 00:03:26,520
for our chubby grandson

75
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:27,690
to nourish his brain.

76
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:30,500
Nourish the brain, so he can be smarter.

77
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,170
Right.

78
00:03:37,079 --> 00:03:37,780
No.

79
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,250
We can't hit him with a car.

80
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:41,090
I... I faint at the sight of blood.

81
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:43,150
A car accident has to involve a car.

82
00:03:43,170 --> 00:03:44,900
What if there aren't enough cars
on the road?

83
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:45,900
How are we supposed to kill him?

84
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,579
The police will see right through it.

85
00:03:47,579 --> 00:03:48,780
Then let's wait till he's drunk

86
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,650
and leave him in the middle of the road.

87
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:51,920
Like last time?

88
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:54,150
You dragged him back halfway there!

89
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:56,360
What if he doesn't get run over
and wakes up?

90
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,360
He'd wake up and find himself sleeping
in the middle of the road!

91
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,560
What would he think happened?

92
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,470
Then who would end up dead? Who?

93
00:04:18,829 --> 00:04:19,750
These days,

94
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:23,040
his father keeps urging him
to chase down contracts every day.

95
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,250
He's out wining and dining every day.

96
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:27,770
We have plenty of chances.

97
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:31,010
Next time he goes out drinking,

98
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,930
we'll pick him up together.

99
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:36,200
We'll dump him
somewhere deserted along the way.

100
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:37,740
We'll hit him first.

101
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,220
Make sure he's dead.

102
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,510
Then we'll run him over.

103
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,500
Crush him to pieces.

104
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:05,120
Leave him there.

105
00:05:05,770 --> 00:05:07,360
Then we leave and go to the hospital.

106
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,620
Later when cops ask,

107
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,770
tell them I had a stomachache halfway.

108
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:13,800
So he told you to take me to emergency.

109
00:05:14,050 --> 00:05:15,580
And he walked home by himself.

110
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,370
There'll be doctors and nurses

111
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:19,660
to testify for us.

112
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,250
We definitely will be fine.

113
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:42,060
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

114
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:35,860
Where are we going?

115
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:37,930
We had a great time... drinking.

116
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:39,500
Perfect.

117
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,560
Come on.

118
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:41,730
Book a room.

119
00:05:42,159 --> 00:05:42,930
Book a room.

120
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:45,740
Why do I get the feeling
that you can hold your liquor better now?

121
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:47,330
You can drink a lot now.

122
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:48,690
-I think you really...
-Dewu.

123
00:05:48,690 --> 00:05:50,250
You can drink a lot now.

124
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:51,090
Quit spinning around.

125
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:52,680
Who?

126
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:53,659
What's going on?

127
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:54,720
Bro, this is...

128
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,870
What's wrong with you?

129
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:56,980
Sorry, bro.

130
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:57,560
You...

131
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,240
Well, this...

132
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,740
Why are you here?

133
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,120
I was worried, so I came to take you home.

134
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,630
I was worried you'd drink too much.
Look at you.

135
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:03,830
I'm pestered by this old woman

136
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:04,870
every day!

137
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:06,000
I have no free time at all!

138
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:06,780
Mrs. Li?

139
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:08,010
Hello, bro.

140
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:10,430
Mrs. Li is so pretty.

141
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:11,810
You're a lucky guy.

142
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:13,710
-Thank you. Thank you.
-She was prettier when she was young.

143
00:06:13,730 --> 00:06:14,630
I'm taking him home.

144
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:16,000
-Let's go.
-She's old now.

145
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:16,930
She's not pretty anymore.

146
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:18,450
-Let's go. The kid is at home.
-I'm not leaving.

147
00:06:18,450 --> 00:06:20,570
I'm treating him to karaoke.

148
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:21,810
Mrs. Li is coming with us, right?

149
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:22,810
-No.
-Mr. Yang. Mr. Yang.

150
00:06:22,810 --> 00:06:24,070
-Sorry.
-No. She's not coming.

151
00:06:24,070 --> 00:06:25,150
I'm taking Mr. Li home.

152
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,240
I'm not leaving!

153
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,830
-I want to sing!
-Bye bye.

154
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:29,120
Go home and keep Mrs. Li company!

155
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,560
Save me a room!

156
00:06:32,130 --> 00:06:34,030
You're staggering. Be careful!

157
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:37,870
Let's go sing.

158
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:40,560
Shasha Hair Salon.

159
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:42,659
Sing. Wash hair.

160
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,070
Sis, I'm not leaving!

161
00:06:47,330 --> 00:06:48,310
Again!

162
00:07:03,830 --> 00:07:05,550
Wash hair.

163
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:08,500
Let's go sing.

164
00:07:22,430 --> 00:07:23,240
Dewu.

165
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:24,250
Pee.

166
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,260
Get off and pee.

167
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:27,000
Hurry, come on.

168
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,000
I didn't say I wanted to pee.

169
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,660
Yes, you did. You said you wanted to pee
as soon as you got in the car.

170
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:31,720
Come on.

171
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:34,270
Pee?

172
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:35,990
Dewu, let's go. Come on.

173
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:39,770
Not... Not here!

174
00:07:39,770 --> 00:07:40,570
Don't, don't, don't!

175
00:07:40,570 --> 00:07:41,870
You... You can't pee here!

176
00:07:41,870 --> 00:07:42,600
It's dark here.

177
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,370
Um... you'll pee on yourself here.

178
00:07:44,370 --> 00:07:46,020
Then where should I pee?

179
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,000
Up ahead. Up ahead.

180
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,380
Over there. There's a tree over there.

181
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,810
So fussy, old woman.

182
00:07:50,810 --> 00:07:53,340
Why are you so fussy?

183
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:54,540
Let's go.

184
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,760
Every day,

185
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:57,240
why are you... why are you...

186
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,040
why are you always wasting money?

187
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:58,560
Let's go.

188
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,340
Every day, you...

189
00:07:59,510 --> 00:08:00,270
So much trouble

190
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:02,020
every day!

191
00:08:02,330 --> 00:08:02,660
Come.

192
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,440
Come, come.

193
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:06,230
Come. Hold on tight.

194
00:08:06,870 --> 00:08:08,060
Pee.

195
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:09,720
Where should I pee?

196
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,810
Over here. Here. Here.

197
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:12,630
Here.

198
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:15,270
I'm going... going home!

199
00:08:15,810 --> 00:08:17,130
-Get lost!
-Come on. Step back a bit.

200
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,060
Here. Here.

201
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:18,510
Here.

202
00:08:18,510 --> 00:08:19,560
Unzip me!

203
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:21,160
Stand still.

204
00:08:21,810 --> 00:08:22,560
Stand still.

205
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:23,620
Hurry up.

206
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:24,390
Okay, you can pee now.

207
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:25,270
Unzip me.

208
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:28,430
Where are you going?

209
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:30,740
Don't run around!

210
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:32,789
I'll beat you to death when we get back.

211
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:38,620
Hit him.

212
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:41,220
Hit him!

213
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:45,740
He's about to finish peeing!

214
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:46,730
Hurry up!

215
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:48,220
Hit him!

216
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,740
What the hell?

217
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:53,050
Step on the gas!

218
00:08:53,050 --> 00:08:54,290
Handbrake! Handbrake!

219
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:57,270
Hit him!

220
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:57,940
Hit him!

221
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:23,650
Pay!

222
00:09:24,470 --> 00:09:25,850
You have to pay for this car.

223
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:28,180
[Hygiene and Health]

224
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:27,910
You have to pay for it!

225
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:29,600
Little bastard.

226
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:31,010
Can you talk like this?

227
00:09:32,390 --> 00:09:33,550
Can you talk?

228
00:09:33,770 --> 00:09:34,270
Yes.

229
00:09:34,890 --> 00:09:35,860
What happened to the car?

230
00:09:35,250 --> 00:09:37,190
[Hygiene and Health]

231
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:36,910
Did it move by itself?

232
00:09:38,290 --> 00:09:39,600
What do you mean?

233
00:09:39,930 --> 00:09:41,710
Did I buy a Transformer?

234
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:42,720
Did it go save the earth by itself?

235
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,360
N-No, no, Mr. Li.

236
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,870
I... I really don't know what happened.

237
00:09:44,870 --> 00:09:46,220
I just wanted to drive the car

238
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,010
forward a bit

239
00:09:47,010 --> 00:09:47,910
to pick you up earlier.

240
00:09:47,910 --> 00:09:48,790
I... I don't know what happened either.

241
00:09:48,790 --> 00:09:50,820
I just heard someone yell in my ear.

242
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:52,530
I got startled, and then...

243
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:54,250
Mr. Li, I really didn't mean to hit you.
Really.

244
00:09:54,250 --> 00:09:55,340
Who yelled at you?

245
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:56,510
I don't know what it was.

246
00:09:56,510 --> 00:09:57,390
The car yelled at you?

247
00:09:57,390 --> 00:09:58,650
No. I just heard it.

248
00:09:58,650 --> 00:09:59,510
Was it Optimus Prime?

249
00:09:59,510 --> 00:10:00,910
-I really... really don't know.
-The car yelled at you?

250
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:02,130
I know, I know.

251
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:06,500
I know what happened.

252
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:12,890
Gods and immortals,

253
00:10:12,890 --> 00:10:14,440
drive away the vengeful spirits for me.

254
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,460
Drive away the vengeful spirits.

255
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:18,960
Vengeful spirits of the East, scatter!

256
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:21,960
Vengeful spirits of the West, begone!

257
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,770
Vengeful spirits of the South, perish!

258
00:10:24,770 --> 00:10:27,890
Vengeful spirits of the North, depart!

259
00:10:27,890 --> 00:10:31,220
Heavenly Soldiers, assemble as ordered!

260
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:34,630
Why hasn't it been driven away
after so long?

261
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:36,130
It's fiercer than the last one
you dealt with.

262
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:37,740
-Fiercer?
-Yeah.

263
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:39,700
Of course it's fiercer.

264
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,630
I almost couldn't handle it.

265
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,170
My goodness.

266
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:51,870
Scatter!

267
00:11:02,510 --> 00:11:02,890
Here.

268
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:05,080
Here, drink it while it's hot.

269
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,960
Is... Is this thing... drinkable?

270
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:07,840
You should drink it quickly.

271
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,390
No, this... this...

272
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,480
What are you thinking? Just drink it.

273
00:11:14,510 --> 00:11:15,860
Master told you to drink it,
so drink it.

274
00:11:18,150 --> 00:11:18,670
Hurry up!

275
00:11:20,130 --> 00:11:20,600
Hurry up!

276
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,340
That's enough.

277
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:28,150
Oh my God.

278
00:11:29,170 --> 00:11:30,140
That should do it.

279
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:30,980
Done?

280
00:11:31,010 --> 00:11:31,660
Oh my God.

281
00:11:33,050 --> 00:11:33,890
Look.

282
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,390
Master, Master.

283
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:38,600
What do you think possessed him?

284
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:40,120
I can't tell you.

285
00:11:41,890 --> 00:11:43,050
It's a vengeful spirit.

286
00:11:43,270 --> 00:11:46,700
I've temporarily hypnotized it.

287
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:47,890
But we can't say its name.

288
00:11:47,890 --> 00:11:48,550
If we say the name,

289
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:49,650
it will wake up again.

290
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:51,080
To protect this man,

291
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,900
I've covered him with a big shield.

292
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,600
Now non-humans can't see him.

293
00:11:54,820 --> 00:11:55,580
He's fine now.

294
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:56,750
He's been covered?

295
00:11:56,750 --> 00:11:57,610
Yes.

296
00:11:58,250 --> 00:11:59,390
Um, um...

297
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:01,750
How did this happen, Ms. Wan?

298
00:12:01,750 --> 00:12:03,270
What has my family done recently?

299
00:12:03,270 --> 00:12:05,080
Things like this happen every few days.

300
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,750
What did we provoke?

301
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:10,200
Born in the Year of the Monkey, right?

302
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,510
No wonder.

303
00:12:19,050 --> 00:12:20,240
No wonder.

304
00:12:20,510 --> 00:12:22,340
What were you two lifetimes ago?

305
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,200
You were a great general.

306
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:25,750
Your heroic spirit still lingers.

307
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:28,950
The ones coming to you
are all your former soldiers.

308
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:30,390
Why do they all come to you?

309
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:32,270
Because you are righteous and kind.

310
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:34,630
Why do they keep coming?

311
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:35,630
Because you didn't just lead

312
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:36,650
one or two soldiers.

313
00:12:36,650 --> 00:12:37,940
You led thousands of them.

314
00:12:38,130 --> 00:12:40,130
Think about it. Am I right?

315
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:40,510
How... How...

316
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:42,000
How can I suppress these...

317
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,800
Ms. Wan, thank you for your hard work.

318
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,170
Please accept this.

319
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,370
What are you doing?

320
00:12:46,370 --> 00:12:48,390
-That's too much.
-No, no. Ms. Wan.

321
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,360
Let's fix this completely this time.

322
00:12:50,630 --> 00:12:51,960
If no one comes to my husband again,

323
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:52,960
he'll be at ease.

324
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:53,460
Right?

325
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:54,870
Yes, it must be fixed completely.

326
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:56,200
Fix this completely. Yes.

327
00:12:56,410 --> 00:12:57,870
Hurry. G-Give all the money to Master.

328
00:12:57,870 --> 00:12:58,960
Don't be stingy.

329
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,150
G-Give all the money to Master.

330
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,270
Give all the money.

331
00:13:01,870 --> 00:13:02,670
Nothing left. Th-That's all we have now.

332
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:04,080
-Of course. I'll fix this completely.
-That's all the money we have now.

333
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,550
Okay, I-I understand. How about this?

334
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:07,640
I'll light longevity lamps for you
in the Buddhist hall.

335
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:08,320
Okay?

336
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:08,620
Thank you.

337
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,250
Thank you. Thank you.

338
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:10,360
-Thank you, Ms. Wan.
-Amitabha.

339
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,130
We... We

340
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:12,000
have been brought together by fate.

341
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:24,890
Hong,

342
00:13:24,890 --> 00:13:25,580
I'm begging you.

343
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:26,840
Let's stop trying to kill him.

344
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:27,820
If you keep doing this,

345
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:29,510
I'll die before him sooner or later.
Really.

346
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:30,770
We'll stop.

347
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:32,500
I've thought about it.

348
00:13:33,050 --> 00:13:34,790
We're not professionals at killing.

349
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,250
After everything we've done,

350
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:37,450
he didn't even get a scratch.

351
00:13:38,010 --> 00:13:38,860
Killing

352
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:40,770
is a job for professionals.

353
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:46,220
Go to the Yuhong Square nightclub.

354
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:47,240
Find Dong

355
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,420
and ask him

356
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:49,660
to take care of Li Dewu.

357
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:51,360
Where did you get this money?

358
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:52,100
From the safe.

359
00:13:52,410 --> 00:13:53,750
How did you know the code?

360
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,050
When Fatty Li gets drunk,

361
00:13:55,050 --> 00:13:56,110
he spills everything.

362
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:57,340
Get it done quickly.

363
00:13:57,370 --> 00:13:58,900
We can't let him find out
the money is missing.

364
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,270
What are you doing here?

365
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:17,600
Looking for...

366
00:14:19,370 --> 00:14:20,410
Looking for Dong.

367
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:21,940
Why are you looking for him?

368
00:14:23,010 --> 00:14:23,870
To talk business.

369
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:28,910
How much is this?

370
00:14:31,650 --> 00:14:33,360
You think 50,000 yuan is enough
to get me to kill someone for you?

371
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:34,750
This...

372
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:36,080
This... This is the... the deposit.

373
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:37,860
Y-You'll get the other half
when the job's done.

374
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:43,320
Who do you want to kill?

375
00:14:44,870 --> 00:14:46,750
The boss of Wenwu Lubricants,

376
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:47,960
Li Dewu.

377
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:50,370
Li Dewu?

378
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:55,590
The one who always goes
to Shasha Hair Salon to wash his hair?

379
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,110
I don't know him.

380
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,700
Someone else asked me to come.

381
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,600
Come on.

382
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:04,200
Aren't you his driver?

383
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,130
You're wearing sunglasses.

384
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,290
Are you going to play Erquan Yingyue?

385
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:12,250
What? You know me?

386
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:14,270
Not only do I know you,

387
00:15:14,270 --> 00:15:16,220
I also know the car you drive.

388
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,290
Every day, you take him out to eat
and get his hair washed.

389
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:19,630
So stop pretending.

390
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,250
Go back and wait for news.

391
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:23,460
I'll let you know when it's done.

392
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,100
Aren't you going
to write a receipt or something?

393
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,550
When did you come in?

394
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:51,550
You came back to steal my money,
didn't you?

395
00:15:51,550 --> 00:15:52,080
No.

396
00:15:53,130 --> 00:15:54,050
I'll take this job.

397
00:15:55,650 --> 00:15:57,250
He is my disease.

398
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:58,210
If he dies,

399
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,540
I'll be cured.

400
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,330
Either he dies

401
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,030
or I do.

402
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:10,430
Hit him!

403
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:23,510
Follow the direction of my soybeans.

404
00:16:23,510 --> 00:16:25,110
Over there!

405
00:16:28,370 --> 00:16:30,710
Over here! Over here!

406
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:32,860
Over here!

407
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:33,750
Over there.

408
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:36,700
Over here. Over here.

409
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:38,870
Over here!

410
00:16:38,870 --> 00:16:40,120
Over here!

411
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:49,870
Is this Li Dewu?

412
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:56,040
I'm from the Municipal Bureau.

413
00:16:56,770 --> 00:16:57,580
And

414
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,240
I'm in charge of your husband's case.

415
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:04,660
When was the last time you saw Li Dewu?

416
00:17:07,790 --> 00:17:09,349
Yesterday... morning.
